{"id":"danube-cycle-path","title":"Danube Cycle Path: Passau to Budapest","who":"Classic route · EuroVelo 6, Europe's favourite river ride","when":"April to October","vehicle":"Any bike (lots of e-bikes), 10–14 days","kind":"bike","color":"#0891b2","summary":"About 630 km downhill along the Danube through Austria, Slovakia and Hungary: the best-signposted, smoothest stretch of EuroVelo 6 to Vienna, the vineyards and abbeys of the Wachau, three capitals, and a quieter, rougher Hungarian half. Easy, social, and good for families. Check the official closure lists before you go: there are signed detours, such as through Mautern until April 2027.","sources":[{"label":"Donauregion Upper Austria: current closures on the Danube Cycle Path","url":"https://donauregion.at/en/closures.html"},{"label":"Epsom CC: Graeme Aston, Regensburg to Budapest (August 2025)","url":"https://www.epsomcc.co.uk/?p=11148"},{"label":"Cycloscope: Danube Cycling Path, the ultimate guide","url":"https://cycloscope.net/danube-cycling-path-map/"}],"approximate":"The usual stages; the line follows cycle paths near the river.","km":612,"bbox":[13.4606,47.4819,19.1451,48.5916],"stops":[{"name":"Passau","place":"Passau, Germany","at":[48.5748,13.461],"text":"The city of three rivers, where the Inn and the Ilz meet the Danube.","source":{"label":"Epsom CC (2025)","url":"https://www.epsomcc.co.uk/?p=11148"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/PassauCollection2025.jpg/500px-PassauCollection2025.jpg","page":"Passau","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PassauCollection2025.jpg","credit":"Compiled by Viceskeeni2","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"Schlögen bend","place":"Schlögen, Austria","at":[48.4239,13.8709],"text":"Into Austria and round the river's great hairpin loop."},{"name":"Linz","place":"Linz, Austria","at":[48.3059,14.2862],"text":"A riverside city of art and technology.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Linz_Blick_von_Freinbergstrasse_32-2_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Linz_Blick_von_Freinbergstrasse_32-2_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Linz","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Linz_Blick_von_Freinbergstrasse_32-2_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Radler59 (talk)","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Grein","place":"Grein, Austria","at":[48.2272,14.8552],"text":"The wooded Strudengau gorge."},{"name":"Melk","place":"Melk, Austria","at":[48.2272,15.337],"text":"The golden baroque abbey high over the river."},{"name":"Wachau","place":"Dürnstein, Austria","at":[48.3954,15.5203],"text":"Apricot orchards and terraced vineyards; Richard the Lionheart's castle ruin above Dürnstein.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Wachau_%282%29.JPG/500px-Wachau_%282%29.JPG","page":"Wachau","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wachau_%282%29.JPG","credit":"C.Stadler/Bwag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Tulln","place":"Tulln an der Donau","at":[48.3312,16.0518],"text":"Flat river meadows towards the capital.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/GuentherZ_2010-04-24_0034_Tulln_Hauptplatz.jpg/500px-GuentherZ_2010-04-24_0034_Tulln_Hauptplatz.jpg","page":"Tulln an der Donau","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GuentherZ_2010-04-24_0034_Tulln_Hauptplatz.jpg","credit":"GuentherZ","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Vienna","place":"Vienna, Austria","at":[48.2084,16.3725],"text":"Coffee houses, palaces, and a rest day well spent.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg/500px-Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg","page":"Vienna","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg","credit":"Superbass","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Bratislava","place":"Bratislava, Slovakia","at":[48.1435,17.1083],"text":"A second capital an hour's ride away, under its castle.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Bratislava_-_Burg_%28b%29.JPG/500px-Bratislava_-_Burg_%28b%29.JPG","page":"Bratislava Castle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bratislava_-_Burg_%28b%29.JPG","credit":"C.Stadler/Bwag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Győr","place":"Győr, Hungary","at":[47.6835,17.6343],"text":"Into Hungary: a baroque town between rivers.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Gy%C5%91r_montage1.jpg/500px-Gy%C5%91r_montage1.jpg","page":"Győr","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gy%C5%91r_montage1.jpg","credit":"SNRTZ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Komárom","place":"Komárom, Hungary","at":[47.7417,18.1218],"text":"Fortresses on both banks, Hungary and Slovakia.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Kom%C3%A1rom_-_Fort_Igm%C3%A1nd.jpg/500px-Kom%C3%A1rom_-_Fort_Igm%C3%A1nd.jpg","page":"Komárom","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kom%C3%A1rom_-_Fort_Igm%C3%A1nd.jpg","credit":"Mediatus","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Esztergom","place":"Esztergom, Hungary","at":[47.7857,18.7403],"text":"Hungary's huge basilica, then the river turns south through the Danube Bend.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Basilica_in_Esztergom%2C_Hungary_01.jpg/500px-Basilica_in_Esztergom%2C_Hungary_01.jpg","page":"Esztergom Basilica","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basilica_in_Esztergom%2C_Hungary_01.jpg","credit":"Pudelek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Budapest","place":"Budapest, Hungary","at":[47.4818,19.1449],"text":"The parliament on the river and a thermal bath to finish.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Hungarian_Parliament_Building_from_across_the_Danube%2C_2025-01-11.jpg/500px-Hungarian_Parliament_Building_from_across_the_Danube%2C_2025-01-11.jpg","page":"Hungarian Parliament Building","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Fi